[A] LINEAR-in-K operator: can delta(c_chi^2) ~ (H/M)^1 (one power)?
    K = extrinsic curvature trace of the T=const leaves = del.u = 3H.
    An operator like (K/M)(del chi)^2 is dim-5 (one power of M).
    BUT: (del chi)^2 = g^ij d_i chi d_j chi is the GRADIENT term whose
    coefficient IS c_chi^2. A term (K/M) h^{ij} d_i chi d_j chi shifts it:
        delta c_chi^2 ~ (K/M) = 3H/M   (ONE power -- larger than (H/M)^2!)
    Is this operator ALLOWED? Check the discrete symmetries:
    - K = del.u changes sign under TIME REVERSAL (u -> -u): K is T-ODD.
    - (del chi)^2 (spatial gradient squared) is T-EVEN.
    => (K/M)(del chi)^2 is T-ODD: FORBIDDEN in a T-invariant (CPT) khronon
       action. The khronon action S_u is built from T-even scalars
       (u.del u)^2, (del u)^2, (del.u)^2 -- all QUADRATIC in u-derivatives,
       hence T-even. A single power of K is T-odd -> not generated.
    -> The leading allowed curvature shift is QUADRATIC: K^2/M^2 ~ (H/M)^2.
       The (H/M)^1 enhancement is SYMMETRY-FORBIDDEN. Back to (H/M)^2.
      [hypothetical, if allowed] 3H/M at M=M_Pl: 1.784e-60
      [hypothetical, if allowed] 3H/M at M=meV (SC floor): 4.344e-30
    even the (forbidden) linear term is 1e-30 (meV) to 1e-60 (M_Pl): still dead.

[B] Is c_chi PROTECTED (does not run) or RADIATIVELY GENERATED?
    c_chi^2 = ratio of c_i couplings. The c_i are marginal (dim-4 operator
    coefficients of (del u)^2). They RUN logarithmically and receive finite
    matching, BUT there is NO symmetry forcing a SPECIFIC value -- they are
    free inputs (like gauge couplings). So c_chi is NOT symmetry-fixed to a
    number; it is a free dimensionless coupling. Radiative corrections shift
    it by O(c_i^2/16pi^2)*log -- a SELF-correction (set by the c_i themselves),
    NOT an H-dependent one. dS only enters through (curvature/M^2) insertions,
    already shown ~ (H/M)^2. => no H-lock from running.

[C] SYMMETRY lock to a FIXED value (c_chi = c = 1)? -- different question
    If a residual symmetry forced c_chi^2 = 1 exactly, that is a lock to a
    CONSTANT, NOT c_chi = f(H). Check: does dS restore boost invariance for
    the khronon? NO -- the khronon EXISTS precisely to break boosts (defines
    a preferred frame). c_T^2=1/(1-beta)=1 is forced by GW170817 (|beta|<1e-15)
    but that is the SPIN-2 (tensor) speed, set by beta. The SPIN-0 speed c_chi
    is a SEPARATE combination (c_123/...) NOT fixed by c_T. agentU banked the
    spin-0 speed FREE in [1.000,1.033]. No symmetry pins it to 1.
    => even a symmetry lock would give c_chi=const, NOT the f(H) the
       edge coincidence needs. It would not help: R(H) still slides vs G_sat(const).

[D] Gibbons-Hawking THERMAL shift: T_dS = H/2pi. Thermal correction to c_chi?
    T_dS = H/2pi = 2.305e-43 GeV.
    Finite-T correction to a sound speed ~ (T/M)^2 (thermal mass / loop):
      (T_dS/M)^2 at M=M_Pl: 8.958e-123
      (T_dS/M)^2 at M=meV (SC floor): 5.311e-62
    Same (H/M)^2 suppression (T_dS ~ H). Thermal route gives NO lock either.

[E] THE DECISIVE SCALE-SEPARATION (the recurring residual, quantified):
    For dS to lock c_chi to H at O(1), the controlling scale M must satisfy
    M ~ H. The khronon EFT cutoff / LV scale obeys M >= M_SC >~ meV.
    log10(M_SC/H) >= 29.84   i.e. M is AT LEAST ~30 orders
    of magnitude above H. (meV/H0_energy = 6.91e+29 = 10^29.8)
    The two scales (c_chi-intrinsic M, and H) are DECOUPLED by >= 30 decades.
    This is EXACTLY the recurring residual: R is H-intrinsic, G_sat/c_chi is
    M-intrinsic (>= meV), and dS curvature cannot bridge a 30-decade gap with
    an (H/M)^2 lever. NO RADIATIVE LOCK.

